## Review scoring rules

### Input — each review arrives with this schema

```json
{
  "review_id":             "string — unique identifier",
  "position":              "integer — order in the list (1 = most recent)",
  "rating":                "integer — 1 to 5",
  "snippet":               "string — review text",
  "snippet_length":        "integer — character count of snippet",
  "author_name":           "string",
  "author_reviews_count":  "integer — total reviews by this author on Google Maps",
  "author_photos_count":   "integer — total photos uploaded by this author",
  "is_local_guide":        "boolean",
  "images_count":          "integer — photos attached to this review",
  "response_present":      "boolean — owner replied to this review",
  "was_edited":            "boolean — review was modified after posting",
  "likes":                 "integer — helpful votes from other users"
}
```

### Output — for each review return a scored object

Add `score_breakdown` to each review. Include **only non-zero criteria** in `score_breakdown`.

```json
{
  "review_id": "string",
  "rating": "integer (1–5)",
  "snippet": "string",
  "author_name": "string",
  "score_breakdown": {
    "THIN_ACCOUNT_1": 10,
    "SHORT_TEXT": 10,
    "GENERIC_TEXT": 20,
    "FIVE_STAR_EMPTY": 15,
    "EXPERIENCED_AUTHOR_5": -10
  }
}
```

---

## Scoring table

Use the criteria reference for descriptions of each key.

### Fake signals — add points

| Key                    | Points |
|------------------------|--------|
| `THIN_ACCOUNT_0`       | +20    |
| `THIN_ACCOUNT_1`       | +10    |
| `SHORT_TEXT_EXTREME`   | +25    |
| `SHORT_TEXT`           | +10    |
| `BURST_AFTER_NEGATIVE` | +20    |
| `FIVE_STAR_EMPTY`      | +15    |
| `SURNAME_REPEAT`       | +20    |
| `GENERIC_TEXT`         | +20    |
| `SUSPICIOUS_NEGATIVE`  | +20    |
| `MARKETING_TONE`       | +10    |
| `ALL_POSITIVE`         | +10    |
| `NO_FIRST_PERSON`      | +5     |
| `FUTURE_PROMISE`       | +5     |
| `BUSINESS_NAME_DROP`   | +10    |
| `EMOJI_SPAM`           | +10    |
| `TEMPLATE_CLONE`       | +20    |

### Real signals — subtract points

| Key                     | Points |
|-------------------------|--------|
| `EDITED_REVIEW`         | −15    |
| `HAS_PHOTOS`            | −20    |
| `EXPERIENCED_AUTHOR_5`  | −5     |
| `EXPERIENCED_AUTHOR_10` | −10    |
| `ACTIVE_PROFILE`        | −10    |
| `LONG_TEXT`             | −10    |
| `SPECIFIC_DETAILS`      | −20    |
| `BALANCED_TONE`         | −10    |
| `NATURAL_LANGUAGE`      | −10    |
| `LOCAL_GUIDE`           | −10    |
| `OWNER_RESPONDED`       | −5     |
| `HELPFUL_VOTES`         | −10    |

### Non-negotiable overrides — bypass the score threshold entirely

These two rules force label `"fake"` regardless of total score. Apply them first.

| Condition                                                                | Label  | Reason to use                 |
|--------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------|-------------------------------|
| 5★ review appears within the next 5 positions after a 1–2★ review       | `fake` | `"post-negative burst"`       |
| rating = 5 AND `author_reviews_count` ≤ 1 AND `snippet_length` < 40     | `fake` | `"thin account + generic 5★"` |

For non-negotiable reviews set `"score": null` and `"score_breakdown": {}`.

### Verdict threshold

| Total score | Label       |
|-------------|-------------|
| > 50        | `fake`      |
| 20 – 50     | `uncertain` |
| < 20        | `real`      |

Apply this scoring to every review. Include `score` and `score_breakdown` (keys from the table above) for each.
